(PART E — LT POWER AND CONTROL CABLES) Tj T*
(\(a\) Power cables shall be 1.1 kV grade, aluminium conductor, XLPE insulated, armoured) Tj T*
(and PVC sheathed, conforming to IS 7098 \(Part 1\):1988.) Tj T*
(\(b\) The cables shall be suitable for a maximum continuous conductor temperature of 90°C.) Tj T*
(\(c\) Control cables shall be PVC insulated, copper conductor of 2.5 sq mm, 1.1 kV grade,) Tj T*
(conforming to IS 1554 \(Part 1\).) Tj T*
(\(d\) Conductors shall be stranded, class 2, conforming to IS 8130.) Tj T*
(\(e\) Cables shall be laid in RCC trenches or on perforated cable trays as shown in the) Tj T*
(drawings.) Tj T*
(\(f\) Cable ends shall be terminated using double compression glands and crimped lugs.) Tj T*
(\(g\) Each drum shall be marked with the manufacturer's name, size, voltage grade and year) Tj T*
(of manufacture.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6 TESTS AND INSPECTION) Tj T*
(\(a\) Routine verification of each assembly shall be carried out in accordance with IS/IEC) Tj T*
(61439-1.) Tj T*
(\(b\) Routine test certificates of cables shall be furnished with each consignment.) Tj T*
(\(c\) The equipment shall be inspected by the Engineer-in-charge at the manufacturer's) Tj T*
(works before dispatch.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7 DOCUMENTATION, WARRANTY AND TRAINING) Tj T*
(\(a\) The contractor shall submit detailed shop drawings for approval within 21 days of) Tj T*
(award of work.) Tj T*
(\(b\) Three sets of operation and maintenance manuals shall be handed over on completion.) Tj T*
(\(c\) The complete installation shall be guaranteed against defective design, material and) Tj T*
(workmanship for a period of 12 months from the date of handing over.) Tj T*
(\(d\) The contractor shall train the Department's operating staff in operation and routine) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Signature of Bidder) Tj T*
(Page 3 of 4) Tj T*
